$ physa 
exit 2
--- stdout
--- stderr
usage: physa <command> [--help]

Physa: product management for agents.

Commands:
  check     Check the map and the changes of a range against it.
  map       Read the map: a bare map prints the index.
  init      Build the map of a repo, never bounded: it estimates its cost and asks first; with --write, commit it to physa/init; --gather, --propose or --recover runs one phase.
  idea      Add, list and show ideas: a bare idea lists them. An idea belongs to the person who adds it; its facts say where it stands. A slug left out is chosen from a list on a terminal.
  pursue    Pursue an idea: put your name on building it, against a signal of four parts (claim, direction, window, resolver). On a terminal the signal is written in $VISUAL or $EDITOR; --signal-from reads it from a file, or stdin for -, and off a terminal it is required. --appetite sets a budget in tokens; with none there is no circuit breaker, and spend is still counted. Only a person pursues: inside an agent's session it is refused. A slug left out is chosen from a list on a terminal.
  pursuit   List, show and stop pursuits, set and show a pursuit's plan, and say which change a session works on. Only a person stops a pursuit: inside an agent's session it is refused. A slug left out is chosen from a list on a terminal.
  evidence  List the facts observed in version control and the forge, newest first: changes landed and reverted, a merged PR's lead time and its CI result. It reads what the engine stored and polls nothing.
  engine    Start, check and stop the machine's one engine: a bare engine prints its status. status and the api commands start the engine when it is not running; stop never does.
  api       Call the engine's API by name, for debugging: a bare api lists its methods. Each command starts the engine when it is not running.
  sync      Not built yet: it returns with digests, after the engine.
  version   Print the version of this build.
  help      Print the commands.

