$ physa map --help
exit 0
--- stdout
usage: physa map
       physa map index [dir]
       physa map slice <capability>... [--with decisions|questions|all] [--format md|json]
       physa map slice --entry <slug>... [--format md|json]
       physa map changes [<range>] [--json] [--strict]
       physa map records [--json]
       physa map fmt [--check] [dir]
       physa map learn [--signals] [--write [--push [--pr]]] [--since <change>] [--appetite <tokens>] [--agent <name>] [--json]
       physa map hooks

Read the map: a bare map prints the index.

Commands:
  index    List the capabilities of the map with their promises.
  slice    Print the slice of the map a task needs.
  changes  List the capability each change of a range names, with the findings.
  records  List the slice records, newest first.
  fmt      Rewrite the map's folders to their format: contents, index links and spacing (--check writes nothing and exits 1 when a file would change).
  learn    Find what the merged changes have to teach the map, and draft proposals from it for the stewards to review (--signals stops at the signals; --write commits the kept proposals to physa/learn, --push pushes it, --pr opens its PR).
  hooks    Point the repo's hooks at the one that stamps Session: on commits made in Claude Code, so learning can join a change to its session.
--- stderr

