$ physa pursuit --help
exit 0
--- stdout
usage: physa pursuit [list] [--json]
       physa pursuit show [<slug>] [--json]
       physa pursuit stop [<slug>] [--reason <text>] [--yes] [--json]
       physa pursuit plan set [<pursuit>] [--reason <text>] [--from <file>|-] [--json]
       physa pursuit plan show [<pursuit>] [--history] [--json]
       physa pursuit work <pursuit>/<change> [--json]

List, show and stop pursuits, set and show a pursuit's plan, and say which change a session works on. Only a person stops a pursuit: inside an agent's session it is refused. A slug left out is chosen from a list on a terminal.

Commands:
  list  List the pursuits, newest first, with their appetite and what is spent.
  show  Show a pursuit: its facts, its signal, its progress as facts and what needs its person.
  stop  Stop an active pursuit, asking first on a terminal unless --yes.
  plan  Set and show a pursuit's plan: the changes it will land, each in one capability, with what to do and how to tell it is done.
  work  Record that this agent session works on a planned change, so its commits carry a Change: trailer. --current prints <pursuit>/<change> for the session, or nothing; it reads the store and never fails.
--- stderr

