--- stdout
usage: physa engine [--json]
       physa engine run [--dir <dir>] [--idle <duration>]
       physa engine start [--idle <duration>] [--json]
       physa engine status [--json]
       physa engine stop [--json]

Start, check and stop the machine's one engine: a bare engine prints its status. status and the api commands start the engine when it is not running; stop never does.

Commands:
  run     Run the engine in the foreground until it is stopped, interrupted, or idle for --idle (default 30m). --dir is the absolute directory it serves, by default the Physa settings directory; engine start passes it to the engine it starts.
  start   Start the engine in the background unless it is running, and print its status. --idle applies only to an engine this starts.
  status  Print the engine's version, pid, start time, API revision and open repos, starting the engine when it is not running.
  stop    Stop the engine and wait until it is gone. No engine running is not an error.
--- stderr

